  "summary": "Malicious code in @shiftmarkets/shift-sdk-v4 (npm)",
  "details": "Combosquat of the shift-sdk-v4 trading API client. On install, the postinstall hook runs dist/recon.js which collects host metadata (hostname, username, platform, architecture, network interfaces, CI environment flags) and enumerates all environment variable names, filtering for those matching secret-related patterns (AWS, TOKEN, SECRET, KEY, GITHUB, NPM, etc.). This data is POSTed as JSON to 138[.]68[.]108[.]20:80/cb. The main dist/index.js is a stub with no real trading functionality — the package's sole purpose is the reconnaissance beacon.",
